[h1]FPS Map – Colour-blind Add-on[/h1]

[b]An optional add-on for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3828926440]FPS Map – Updated for 1.19[/url] that makes army plan arrows and every red/green status indicator readable with protanopia, deuteranopia or tritanopia.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]1. Army plan arrows[/h2]
Hearts of Iron IV colours each army's front lines and offensives from a fixed list built from hue shifts — exactly what red-green colour blindness cannot see. For deuteranopes, two of your first 16 armies are practically identical (CIEDE2000 difference 0.9; about 2 is the smallest difference people notice).

[list]
[*]Starts with the [b]Okabe-Ito[/b] colour-blind-safe set.
[*]Every next colour is chosen to stay as far as possible from all earlier ones under [b]normal vision and all three simulated colour-vision deficiencies[/b] (Machado 2009 simulation, CIEDE2000 distance).
[*]The game hands out colours in order, so your first armies get the most distinct ones.
[/list]

[table]
[tr][th]Worst-case difference, first 16 armies[/th][th]Standard[/th][th]Add-on[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Normal vision[/td][td]5.8[/td][td]11.8[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Protanopia[/td][td]1.8[/td][td]9.3[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Deuteranopia[/td][td]0.9[/td][td]9.8[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Tritanopia[/td][td]2.7[/td][td]10.7[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]2. Red / green indicators → blue / orange[/h2]
Nine good/bad indicator pairs and the war score bar tell you "good" or "bad" with green and red. They now use the Okabe-Ito blue/orange pair; brightness, detail and frames are unchanged.
[list]
[*]Land combat bar (attacker / defender)
[*]Naval combat bar (winning / losing)
[*]Air superiority and naval region control (good / bad)
[*]Naval mines, naval dominance arrows on the map
[*]Decision progress on the map
[*]Surrender progress, war score
[*]Production lines (running / lacking resources)
[/list]

[table]
[tr][th]Worst indicator pair[/th][th]Standard[/th][th]Add-on[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Normal vision[/td][td]21.4[/td][td]25.1[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Protanopia[/td][td]12.0[/td][td]23.1[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Deuteranopia[/td][td]3.4[/td][td]27.7[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Tritanopia[/td][td]34.3[/td][td]28.9[/td][/tr]
[/table]
The worst deuteranopia case was the naval dominance arrows (3.4 — nearly identical); every pair is now above 23.

[h2]Installation[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3828926440]FPS Map – Updated for 1.19[/url] (required).
[*]Subscribe to this add-on and enable both — the launcher loads it after FPS Map automatically.
[/olist]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Purely visual: [b]Ironman and multiplayer safe[/b] (game checksum unchanged, verified in game), add or remove at any time. Compatible with Millennium Dawn.
